cant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUI CHEMICALS INC</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIYAMA SHINICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUWAHARA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUI CHEMICALS, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIYAMA, SHINICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUWAHARA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIYAMA SHINICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUWAHARA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIYAMA, SHINICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Benzenesulfonic acid derivatives which are utilizable as a dopant for electron-conjugated polymers and are represented by general formula (3) wherein X is hydrogen or hydroxy and R3 and R4 each is hydrogen, alkyl, etc. Examples of the derivatives include 3-sulfobenzamide, 3-sulfobenzoylurea, N-methyl-3-sulfobenzamide, and 5-sulfosalicylamide. Doping an electron-conjugated polymer with any of these compounds gives a conductive polymeric material which has high conductivity and excellent heat resistance and is usable as a conductive cathode material for solid electrolytic capacitors.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des dérivés d'acide benzènesulfonique lesquels sont utilisables comme dopant pour des polymères conjugués à des électrons et sont représentés par la formule générale (3) dans laquelle X représente hydrogène ou hydroxy et R3 ainsi que R4 représentent chacun hydrogène, alkyle, etc. On peut citer à titre d'exemples des dérivés 3-sulfobenzamide, 3-sulfobenzoylurée, N-méthyl-3-sulfobenzamide et 5-sulfosalicylamide. Le fait de doper un polymère conjugué à des électrons avec n'importe lequel de ces composés donne un matériau polymère conducteur présentant une conductivité élevée et une excellente résistance à la chaleur, et utilisable comme matériau de cathode conducteur pour des condensateurs électrolytiques solides.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>